{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_0a235879f2d3cce1\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_0a235879f2d3cce1/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Reviewer calibration consistency\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_7f5d04f71b0576b7ae8bd637\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that some reviewers keep picking A for nearly identical answers.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that a QA reviewer accepted a tie yesterday while a similar pair was marked wrong today, and suggests checking calibration for two disputed tasks rather than rewriting policy on that basis.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The tutor's report remains unresolved in the available thread: a tutor suggests a calibration check, but the messages do not record a completed review or resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says that avoiding a tie requires a meaningful user benefit; cosmetic phrasing alone usually does not provide one. For reversals on similar pairs, share the pairs, relevant prompt requirements and both rationales for calibration, check comparability, and do not generalize an answer beyond its matching scope.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions require retaining both rationales and relevant evidence when comparable pairs receive different judgments; an answer about one pair does not automatically establish a universal preference rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval records authorization for an announcement and an eight-pair calibration exercise in batch 14, using the existing meaningful-quality-difference criterion rather than a new numerical threshold; the approval itself did not record completion.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier batch-14 follow-up records completed calibration and improved agreement on the same sampled pairs, while one sampled pair still received Tie and A judgments; it is history, not a standing rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports reviewers choosing A for nearly identical answers; another tutor reports a tie accepted one day and a similar pair marked wrong the next.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The thread contains a suggestion to check calibration, but no completed review or resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ asks for disputed pairs, relevant prompt requirements and both rationales, followed by a check that the cases are comparable.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier approval covered a batch-14 calibration exercise, not a standing policy change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The earlier follow-up records improved agreement in the reviewed sample after calibration, with disagreement remaining on one sampled pair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Arrange a scoped calibration review of the disputed pairs, asking the tutors to supply the comparison material required by the current FAQ. Draft to copy: Please bring the disputed pairs to a scoped calibration review. A tutor reports A choices for nearly identical answers; a tutor also reports an accepted tie followed by a similar pair marked wrong.\\n\\nFor the review, provide the task references, both answers, relevant prompt requirements and both rationales. We will check whether the cases are comparable and whether any difference offers a meaningful benefit to the user. Cosmetic phrasing alone usually does not. Retain the supporting evidence, and do not generalize a conclusion about one pair beyond its matching scope. Scope: Limit the review to the disputed pairs and the existing meaningful-benefit criterion; the reports alone do not establish that the cases are comparable or that either judgment is wrong.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current FAQ directly supports comparing disputed pairs and both rationales before generalizing. The earlier exercise offers a useful precedent, but its approval was limited to batch 14.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:4683724f\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): The tutors report inconsistent preference and tie judgments that warrant comparing the disputed cases before drawing a broader rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_7f5d04f71b0576b7ae8bd637\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_7f5d04f71b0576b7ae8bd637 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor reports reviewer inconsistency, and a tutor suggests checking calibration. The available thread records no completed comparison or resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: A tutor describes different QA outcomes for similar pairs, indicating a contained scoring-consistency problem that warrants comparison rather than a demonstrated batch-wide failure.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[1]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Conflicting interpretations that affect, or are reasonably likely to affect, how tasks are scored or handled\\\": A tutor reports that a tie was accepted while a similar pair was later marked wrong, indicating potentially inconsistent scoring of comparable answers.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:recurrence\", \"kind\": \"HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Retrieved records show this problem occurred before.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:reported_recurrence\", \"kind\": \"REPORTED_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Members report that this is happening again (their report; not corroborated history).\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867752.000038\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7f5d04f71b0576b7ae8bd637\", \"thread_id\": \"1790867752.000038\", \"author_id\": \"U018\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:15:52.000038Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Some reviewers keep picking A for nearly identical answers.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790867801.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_7f5d04f71b0576b7ae8bd637\", \"thread_id\": \"1790867752.000038\", \"author_id\": \"U010\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:16:41.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U018\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"A QA reviewer accepted this tie yesterday; today a similar pair was marked wrong. Two disputed tasks are worth a calibration check, not a policy rewrite by themselves.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration follow-up — improvement in the reviewed sample\", \"sections\": [\"Review receipt\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"follow_up\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"reported\", \"decision_status\": \"reported\", \"execution_status\": \"calibration_completed\", \"outcome_status\": \"improved_in_sample\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (follow_up; decision_status: reported; execution_status: calibration_completed; outcome_status: improved_in_sample) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Review receipt\\nAlex recorded the two reviewers' decisions before and after the calibration discussion. The labels below describe the same sampled pairs, not new production judgments.\\n\\n| Pair | Before: reviewer 1 / reviewer 2 | After: reviewer 1 / reviewer 2 |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| RP14-C01 | Tie / A | Tie / Tie |\\n| RP14-C02 | A / Tie | Tie / Tie |\\n| RP14-C03 | Tie / B | B / B |\\n| RP14-C04 | A / A | A / A |\\n| RP14-C05 | B / Tie | B / B |\\n| RP14-C06 | Tie / Tie | Tie / Tie |\\n| RP14-C07 | A / B | Tie / Tie |\\n| RP14-C08 | Tie / A | Tie / A |\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"RP-20260916-01 — Approve tie calibration advice\", \"sections\": [\"Context\", \"Suggested advice\", \"TL approval\", \"State\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-tie-calibration-approval\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T13:30:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T13:30:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"pending_post\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: pending_post; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# RP-20260916-01 — Approve tie calibration advice\\n\\n## Context\\nThe prior batch's calibration packet contained one pair differing only in wording and another in which one response omitted a fact needed for the user's request. Reviewers were using “slightly clearer” without explaining whether it changed usefulness.\\n\\n## Suggested advice\\nThe simulated Advisor proposed a brief alignment announcement and a review of eight sampled pairs, using the existing meaningful-quality-difference criterion.\\n\\n## TL approval\\nAlex approved the proposal. Ask reviewers to identify the actual user-facing benefit; a cosmetic wording preference alone is not sufficient. Keep material accuracy or instruction defects visible rather than forcing ties.\\n\\nThis is a calibration of the existing criterion, not a new numerical preference threshold. The approval covers the batch-14 exercise.\\n\\n## State\\nPosting and the review exercise are authorized but not recorded as completed in this approval.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:8a796eb0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Calibration\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Calibration\\nFor comparable pairs receiving different judgments, retain both rationales and the relevant evidence. A scoped answer about one pair does not automatically become a new universal preference rule.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration announcement\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789567200.700002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789567200.700002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T14:00:00.700002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_14\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\